n | \\Sigma_{\\prime}^- with independent upper run. The detached head with pale left entry, body, minus and single undotted short index are preserved. Main glyph is his hand; only the independent-upper-run candidate retains undetermined upper-run hand. The exact later primary remains unmarked under S01; the following sentence point stays outside. Complete que with its open q loop, full long descender, joined u/e and one separate triangular point to the right of the descender, through exact B025-G09. Je dis precedes outside the group. The word is firm, his hand; only the separate point retains unresolved hand, role, attachment and surface origin. The whole source group keeps its original qualifier."}}
